#!/bin/bash
# A designer's review of what a change looks like, from Claude Opus 5.5
# (Ben, 2026-11-19, of a new app's first pictures: "omg so much is ugly
# make sure you get visual design reviews from opus 5.5 and astra 6.2";
# the other look is Gemini 4 Neon's now). Beside tools/dev/agy-look:
# every change's pictures go to both before it's committed. Where
# agy-look hunts what's wrong by a pixel, this judges the design: what
# the eye lands on, hierarchy, rhythm, colour, what looks amateur or
# unfinished, and what to do about each, most important first.
#
#   tools/dev/opus-look [--about "WHAT IT IS, WHAT CHANGED"] PICTURE.png…
#
# PICTUREs: the change's pictures (headless: tools/dev/tsession shot),
# each state, look and scale worth judging, in a folder of yours under
# /var/tmp; whole windows, and crops enlarged where detail matters (it
# can only look: it can't crop for itself). It prints its review and
# writes it to opus-look.md beside the first picture (what it did, to
# opus-look.log). Check each thing it says against the pictures
# yourself, fix what's real, and say in the commit what it found and
# what you did.
#
# The review is the Claude CLI in a tmux session, as every agent here
# is (`tools/dev/agents look --by opus`: this is that; Ben, 2026-11-22:
# "always do it through tmux never a script that just goes silent"), so
# it can be read while it looks (`tools/dev/agents peek opus-FOLDER`)
# and told more (`agents say`). Run this in the background: it prints a
# line a minute of what the review is doing, and returns when the
# review is written (0), or as soon as it needs you (3: answer it, then
# run this again with the same pictures to go on waiting). It works
# from the pictures' folder, not the repository, with the tools to read
# and write files there and no other: nothing of the project is loaded,
# nothing can be run.
exec /usr/bin/python3 "$(dirname "$0")/agents" look --by opus "$@"
